Plan2001-O is an experimental object-native operating-system project.
Its source snapshot was imported without prior Git ancestry from the
Plan2001 O-only proof-of-concept branch. It is derived through Plan2001
from Plan 9 and the 9front source tree. Source provenance does not
imply that inherited components were authored by this project.

Plan 9 originated at Bell Labs and was distributed under the Lucent
Public License, Version 1.02. On March 23, 2021, Nokia announced the
transfer of Plan 9 copyrights to the Plan 9 Foundation, which
relicensed Plan 9 under the MIT license reproduced above. The 9front
project's additions and modifications are likewise MIT-licensed.

Plan2001 and Plan2001-O additions and modifications by Petteri Reunamo
are provided under the same MIT license. Preserve upstream copyright,
license and attribution notices in derived files and distributions.
The project architecture, repository layout and build method do not
alter the rights or license obligations of inherited source code.
